  "story": {
    "auto": [
      {
        "text": "Six cargo: preload, three from the ring on its side, two by the terminal. It planned last shots from farther back, so partners could leave.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s18",
          "s16"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Off-season interview: a defensive routine at regionals and championship collected five and dispersed two opponent cargo into the truss.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A post that reads as the team's: a steal auto dialed in on the practice field.",
        "basis": "observer",
        "src": [
          "s21"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "cycle": [
      {
        "text": "In an off-season interview: the driver has two buttons, intake left and intake right; sensors store own cargo and pass opponent cargo straight out the other side.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Flywheel speed and hood angle are interpolated from the distance to the target.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "endgame": [
      {
        "text": "In season it used the high rung, about 5 s.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s16"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "An off-season interview shows the climb: the belted arm takes the mid rung, pistons tilt it back to the high rung, then a second static hook takes the traversal.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s20"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "gave_up": [
      {
        "text": "Traversal: about 15 s against 5 s for the high rung, and after the climber was turned around before the championship it swung too much to be reliable. The team says the extra time could go to cargo, and that only ranking points were lost since its alliance partners could traverse.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s16"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "changed": [
      {
        "text": "An oversight in CAD first made the climber extend past the 16 in limit. With three people on CAD it was harder to get every design right.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s16"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In an off-season interview: a first single-intake design became two to make autos easier, and shooting on the move was added before the championship.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After the championship the team planned to make the climber traverse for the off-season.",
        "basis": "team",
        "src": [
          "s16"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outcome": [
      {
        "text": "49-12-0 in official play; won the Roebling division; captain of the Roebling alliance on Einstein; ranked 15 of the pooled top 20 (OPR 57.73, Roebling).",
        "basis": "record",
        "src": [
          "s1",
          "s2"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "functions": [
    {
      "name": "Drivetrain",
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Counter defense, open more auto paths, and aim easily without a turret",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "drive",
        "structure"
      ],
      "type": "swerve",
      "serves": [],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Four MK4i modules with blue nitrile tread and eight Falcon 500s",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Base 31 x 25 in, described as easy to turn and an optimal fit for a double traversal climb",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Intakes",
      "pieces": [
        "cargo"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Avoid the jams and inconsistency seen when indexing an earlier game's pieces, by sending cargo into the gut one at a time",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cost": [
        {
          "text": "In an off-season interview: mecanum vectoring was reliable after about 20 iterations, but the team would not recommend it to others",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "acquire"
      ],
      "type": "two full-width four-bar intakes with mecanum vectoring",
      "serves": [
        "hub-upper"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Two intakes allow color sorting and make cargo easier to find",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Each runs on one Falcon 500; 3 in compliant wheels pick up, 2 in mecanum wheels vector cargo against a backplate",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Four-bar arms are shaped into hard stops at both ends; pneumatic cylinders stow them",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "1/4 in polycarbonate, with 1/8 in aluminum at the motor mount to prevent belt skipping",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season interview: width of each, about",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ],
          "value": 30.5,
          "unit": "in"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Gut",
      "pieces": [
        "cargo"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Track and control each cargo, and get rid of opponent cargo",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6",
            "s20"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "transfer",
        "retain",
        "sense"
      ],
      "type": "two-run belt path with pass-through color sorting",
      "serves": [
        "hub-upper"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Vertical and horizontal belt runs, powered separately by two Falcon 500s",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Beam breaks track cargo; a color sensor filters opponent cargo",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In an off-season interview: single-sided belts move a ball through and out the far side, or lift and store it",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Off-season interview: code can collect only opponent cargo and put it in chosen places; the team had never needed it",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s20"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dual flywheel launcher",
      "pieces": [
        "cargo"
      ],
      "solves": [
        {
          "text": "Minimize backspin so that cargo does not bounce out of the hub",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "does": [
        "deliver"
      ],
      "type": "dual flywheel shooter",
      "serves": [
        "hub-upper"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "2 in top wheel and 4 in bottom wheel geared to the same surface speed, two Falcon 500s at 1:1",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A 2 in kick wheel keeps constant contact with cargo",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A 4 in brass flywheel on a 2.16:1 upduction makes shots more consistent",
          "basis": "team",
          "src": [
            "s6"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
